```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class StallTotal {
    // Bills of an imagined weekly-market stall; the entries end with 0
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        int count = 0, total = 0, highest = 0;
        System.out.println("Enter the bills, 0 to stop:");
        while (true) {
            int bill = sc.nextInt();
            if (bill == 0)
                break;             // 0 ends the entries
            if (bill < 0)
                continue;          // a negative bill is a mistake: skip it
            count++;
            total += bill;
            if (bill > highest)
                highest = bill;
        }
        System.out.println("Valid bills = " + count);
        System.out.println("Total sale = " + total);
        System.out.println("Highest bill = " + highest);
    }
}
```

**Sample input:** `120 -50 340 75 0`

**Output:**

```
Enter the bills, 0 to stop:
Valid bills = 3
Total sale = 535
Highest bill = 340
```

**Another run, input** `0`**:**

```
Enter the bills, 0 to stop:
Valid bills = 0
Total sale = 0
Highest bill = 0
```

**Variable description**

| Variable | Data type | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| count | int | number of valid bills |
| total | int | sum of the valid bills |
| highest | int | largest valid bill so far |
| bill | int | bill typed by the user |

